      "writtenOn": "2017-05-03T02:03:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Same as line #73: it seems to me that this Pom class models two things: a Maven pom and its generated Android.mk module.\n\nThe comment from line 73 could arguably be considered pedantic, but for here, some pom\u0027s do generate several artifacts. They probably also set the Classifier (which is another coordinate similar to Version) on each artifact to distinguish between them.\n\nI could theoretically see it making sense to split this class into three: MavenArtifact (which models the .jar file), MavenPom (which models the .pom file), and AndroidMkModule (which models the mk module), although in practice I imagine it\u0027d be fine to just skip the AndroidMkModule and just have MavenArtifact and MavenPom since the MavenArtifact would have all the required properties.",
      "revId": "fdc60c790ddedfb7691128b7b58ccd38e0ac605d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e90c3bd_badb3a4d",
        "filename": "cmd/pom2mk/pom2mk.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074628
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-08T06:26:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I moved Name out to a helper method that calls Rewrite instead of calling Rewrite and storing the result in the struct. I also ended up adding another method to get a string list of makefile dependencies, since we don\u0027t really need to store it, but the calculation was too complicated to do in the template itself.\n\nFor the SrcFile/SrcFileSuffix, I switched those to a \"ArtifactFile\" member that\u0027s the file path the artifact represented by this pom file. (And added a comment to that effect)",
      "parentUuid": "76983286_1ddecd8c",
      "revId": "fdc60c790ddedfb7691128b7b58ccd38e0ac605d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
