        "id": 1137668
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-03T02:03:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could see it making sense for pom2mk to take another parameter telling the file path of the Android.mk to generate, which then would allow pom2mk to copy the Maven artifacts (.jar etc) into the places that are referenced by the generated Android.mk files",
      "revId": "fdc60c790ddedfb7691128b7b58ccd38e0ac605d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a1d375f3_31fad8ad",
        "filename": "cmd/pom2mk/pom2mk.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074628
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-08T06:26:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We\u0027d never want to move the actual jar files (since they\u0027re probably checked into git, and may actually be used as a maven repo as well). The expectation was that the Android.mk would be written into the current directory (all the paths will be relative to the current directory), but it doesn\u0027t actually write to the file in case there\u0027s already a custom Android.mk. In that case, you\u0027d want to write it to something like maven.mk and have Android.mk `include` it.",
      "parentUuid": "a464061e_08708696",
      "revId": "fdc60c790ddedfb7691128b7b58ccd38e0ac605d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dbd66d28_2c37f41e",
        "filename": "cmd/pom2mk/pom2mk.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 126,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137668
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-03T02:03:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there any particular reason for rewriting the artifactId? Is it because they\u0027re probably too verbose, or probably not distinct, or because we already have Android.mk modules that are renamings of Maven poms?\n\nIs this name rewriting something that we intend for users to usually specify or do we intend for setting it to be unusual?",
      "revId": "fdc60c790ddedfb7691128b7b58ccd38e0ac605d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "627882e8_5327fa7a",
        "filename": "cmd/pom2mk/pom2mk.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 126,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074628
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-08T06:26:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For the most part, these already have names, and we have no desire to rename everything. There\u0027s also the problem that our names generally contain more information than the artifactId -- it\u0027s closer to groupId+artifactId+version (but not in that format).\n\nExample 1:\n  Android module (not from maven): android-support-v7-mediarouter\n  groupId: com.android.support\n  artifactId: mediarouter-v7\n  version: 24.0.0    (not necessarily the version in our tree, since we only have one)\n\nExample 2:\n  Android module (not from maven): android-support-v4\n  groupId: com.android.support\n  artifactId: support-v4\n  version: 24.0.0\n\nOthers are more complicated, and may include other information like the variation of the artifact (internal vs external, etc) that isn\u0027t represented in the pom format.\n\nSo I expect that using the rewriting will be the norm instead of the exception -- that\u0027s one reason that the entire command line is embedded in the output file. Then it\u0027s possible to use the same rewriting step the next time you need to regenerate it.\n\n\u003cwe talked a bit offline\u003e I may be interesting to move this into a persistent config file instead, since you\u0027re often going to want to run it with the same arguments in the same directory. But that can be a later improvement if we find that we\u0027re often sharing a substantial part of the configurations. If it\u0027s mostly not common, storing the config in the output file should work well enough (and I expect the use of this tool itself may end up being scripted)",
      "parentUuid": "dbd66d28_2c37f41e",
      "revId": "fdc60c790ddedfb7691128b7b58ccd38e0ac605d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
